  "summary": "The identified studies apply graph-based methods, specifically message passing over relational graphs, to the task of hate speech detection. El-Sayed et al. (2022) report an AUROC of 0.93 on the ToxiBench dataset [V0097]. Gupta et al. (2024) evaluate the same method on ProtMap, achieving an accuracy of 0.72 [V0099]. Haddad et al. (2025) apply the method to FireScope, reporting a test MAE of 0.79 [V0100], while Fischer et al. (2023) report an F1 score of 0.65 using GridWatch [V0098]. For comparison, a non-graph baseline using boosted decision-tree ensembles by Chen et al. (2019) achieved an accuracy of 0.77 on FireScope [V0112].",
